// One entry per menu page (src/nav-map.js). `answers` = the question the screen answers; `read` = what to look at;
// `act` = what a person does there.
export const SCREENS = {
  dashboard: { answers: 'What is waiting for a person today?', read: ['v2.15.301 (Platform Admin, 20 Oct 2026, "Waiting = Inbox"): Waiting for you lists each Layer 4 Inbox kind with its count, the oldest and how many are late; Open goes to the Inbox on that kind. Below, Also: failed jobs, key dates coming up, reference sites not reachable and scholarships to link.', 'Waiting for you: each queue with its icon: review items, scholarships to link and to publish, universities ready to admit and onboarding stopped for a person (v2.15.254), reference sites, key dates and failed jobs, each opening its list.', 'Platform health bar: green, amber or red summary.', 'Layers panel: what each layer handled in the last 24 hours; zero for a day means a stuck job.'], act: ['Click a card to go straight to the work.'] },
  // v2.15.266: the Live activity page is retired; its content is on Coverage & completeness › Progress (see coverage).
  courses: { answers: 'What do we hold for each course, and where did each value come from?', read: ['v2.15.366: the evidence button at the top right of Course detail opens the course\'s whole evidence timeline (reads, page changes, AI fills, admissions and refusals, fee reader, cross-checks, edits, entry requirement reads, scholarship links) in an overlay, full screen on a phone; Course detail shows the course\'s published scholarships again.', 'Filters include "International students" (open to international, domestic only, both, not known).', 'Each value shows its source and evidence; a value changed by hand shows "set by hand".', 'Scholarships on a course: one card per published scholarship linked to this course — value, who it is for, nationalities, closing date, provider page and saving per year; More shows the fee after the scholarship and why it is linked. Student nationality narrows the cards to those that name that nationality or are open to any. Only published scholarships are shown. The saving comes from the provider\'s annual international fee; for an Australian course without one it is estimated from the registered CRICOS course cost (total ÷ years) and marked as an estimate (Decision 247). This is the same list search, the website and Zoho receive; it is refreshed every 15 minutes and fully each night.', 'Tuition from the course page (international) is the fee read from the course page; the Registered CRICOS course cost below it is the regulator\'s record. They are two different values, not a duplicate.'], act: ['Check scholarships for this course (Operator and above): reads the provider\'s scholarship pages again through the scraper and attaches those whose page covers the course; the task lists what was added or removed.', 'Edit a course (Curator and above). Your change is locked against automation until you release it.', 'Course links: official page, handbook, international page, how to apply, admission centre, regulator listing.'] },
  providers: { answers: 'Who are the providers, and what do we know about each?', read: ['Provider record: details, who can apply, World rankings (QS and THE by edition), outcomes and scholarships.', 'Academic entry requirements (v2.15.361, v2.15.362; read only here, managed in Catalogue › Entry requirements since v2.15.363): the provider\'s published entry rows by country, level and status, each with its quote and source; Sources and reads lists each official source (web page, PDF or a page read rendered) with its latest read, so a held PDF, a refused page or a page with no row shows with its reason. Read only: rows are admitted in Layer 4.', 'Type (each row, v2.15.276): the institution type from the register rules — TEQSA National Register category, CRICOS institution type, NZQA organisation type and the provider\'s courses (Settings › Pipeline settings › Institution type rules). Needs type means no rule matched; hover for the reason. PIM Admin and above can choose a type by hand (kept, marked set by hand) or Auto to return it to the rules; no reason asked. Canada has no rules yet.', 'Published switch (each row of the list; PIM Operator and above, no reason asked): every active provider is published by default. Switching one off hides it and its courses, campuses and scholarships from Wix, Zoho and the website, greys the row, and pauses its background work (site and page finding, page reads, AI matching, link search, provider facts, scholarships and contact reads). Work a Platform Admin starts by hand still runs, so the record can be fixed before it is published again; switching it back on resumes everything.', 'Archived (Providers › Archived; Curator and above to view, PIM Operator and above to restore): archived providers and courses that are not active, each with why — left the register, archived by hand, closed or merged at the departure review, outside the import scope (Layer 1) or suspended — and when. Archived means unpublished and hidden from the lists, search, Wix, Zoho and the website, with background work stopped. Tick several to restore them together (up to 200 at a time). The Providers and Courses lists show active records unless another Status is chosen. A provider whose registered courses have all left the register is archived automatically and restored automatically if one comes back; the departure still waits in Layer 4 › Inbox (Provider left the register) to record a closure or a merger.', 'Archive a provider by hand (provider panel, PIM Operator and above): Archive provider… shows a checklist of what happens — courses, campuses and scholarships hidden; its adapter and course link search switched off; Layer 4 reviews waiting for it closed as superseded; background work stopped — then asks for a reason from a short list. Restore switches back on exactly what was switched off and reopens those reviews.', 'Campuses, Logos & assets and Archived tabs. Onboarding moved to Layer 2 › Onboarding in v2.15.258.', 'Onboarding (Layer 2 › Onboarding since v2.15.258; v2.15.253, Curator and above to view; Platform Admin to act): every university without an admitting adapter is onboarded automatically, a step at a time: website, course pages, 6 sample pages, the AI proposes the adapter, save in testing and apply, qualify, attach central pages. It then stops at Ready to admit (since v2.15.258 the scholarships are found only after it is admitted and its courses enriched): admitting stays a person\'s step on Layer 2 › Adapters, and a passing check never admits by itself. New universities start by themselves when they are added (a setting). The tiles count Waiting (queued), In progress, Stopped, Ready to admit, Done, universities still without an adapter and central page approvals waiting; press a tile to show those rows. Each row shows the university (opens it in the Adapter builder), its step, a plain note, pages read against courses, the fields ready to admit and why others are held, and new scholarships found. The list refreshes every 30 seconds while universities are in progress.', 'When no field passes (v2.15.255), the AI proposes the settings again, told which fields did not pass and why: an adapter built earlier gets up to two AI attempts (6, then 10 sample pages) and a new one a second attempt with 10. Each proposal is saved in testing, applied and qualified again; nothing is admitted. If still nothing passes, the row shows Needs a person (its own tile), not Ready to admit. The scholarship search runs once per onboarding.', 'Journey (each row, v2.15.255): every step with its time and note, the tasks it ran (course-page search, Fill in from website, scholarship search), each AI draft (sample pages, model, cost), the qualification of each field (read on, agrees, passes or why not), and the scholarships found with their state. New scholarships counts live: found since onboarding started, published, and pages still waiting for the AI.', 'Why onboarding stops, and what to do: No website — enter it in the Adapter builder (1.1); onboarding carries on by itself once a website is recorded. Too few course pages — find or add course pages (Adapter builder 2.1), then Retry. Sample pages not captured — check the site opens and Firecrawl credits remain, then Retry. AI proposal failed — check the OpenRouter credit and the adapter AI allowance, then Retry, or build the adapter by hand. Adapter switched off — someone switched it off on Layer 2 › Adapters; switch it on if that was a mistake, then Retry. Course-page search switched off (v2.15.254) — a person switched off the search for this website; check the website in the Adapter builder (1.1), where a different website replaces the search, then Retry (a search switched off because it was for another domain is replaced by itself). Approve central pages (v2.15.256) — nothing passed on the course pages, so the AI read the university\'s English language policy and academic calendar pages; approve or reject each in the Adapter builder (1.3) or under Approvals waiting, and onboarding moves on to Enrich courses once one is approved. Needs a person (v2.15.255) — nothing passed after the AI attempts: mark the values on the sample pages in the Adapter builder or approve its central pages (1.3), then Retry; admitting by hand also finishes onboarding. Unexpected error — read the note and Retry; if it stops again, open the Adapter builder. Waiting for courses means the university has no active course yet.', 'Approvals waiting (all universities; Pipeline Operator and above to view, Platform Admin to decide): the fee schedules, English policies and academic calendars read from each university\'s central pages, in one place (one university at a time: Adapter builder, step 1.3). Fee schedules and policies follow the country chosen at the top of the section; fee schedules are matched to courses by CRICOS code, so they cover Australian providers only. Academic calendars give the month each study period (Semester 1, Trimester 2, Term 3) starts; they are used only to turn a course page that gives its start as a study period into that month, and never add a start to a course whose page names none. An English policy shows its default score for undergraduate and postgraduate coursework courses, any courses it names with their own score, warnings, and how many course pages agree or differ; a policy that sets scores by English band, by faculty or only on each course page has no default.', 'Filter by country, then by state or territory (Australia), province or territory (Canada) or region (New Zealand). New Zealand regions come from each provider\'s town; a provider whose town is overseas or names two places has no region until one is set on its record.'], act: ['Onboarding (Platform Admin, each with a reason kept in the log): tick rows, then Retry selected (stopped rows only; they start again at the step that stopped) or Stop selected; Onboard all without an adapter queues every university without one, largest first; Onboarding settings switch it on or off, start new universities by themselves, set how many run at once (0 pauses new starts) and run the steps under your own sign-in.', 'Approve or reject a university\'s fee schedule (Platform Admin): approval adds a fee only to courses with none and lists (does not change) a different fee on record. Review rows shows every row first; tick several and choose Approve selected; a schedule with nothing to add is closed with Close (nothing to add).', 'Approve or reject a university\'s English policy (Platform Admin): Review courses lists what approval does to each course. Approval gives the policy\'s score only to courses with no English requirement, no review open and no page still to read; research degrees, double degrees, other levels and courses the policy names are held back. A default that most course pages disagree with (at least 10 compared) cannot be approved. Approving one document of a university closes its other waiting documents of the same kind.', 'Academic calendars (Platform Admin): each university is one row with Intake 1, Intake 2 and the raw value captured from its calendar page; where the page gave no months, enter them by hand with the calendar page address (Save months). Courses with intakes already, or set by hand, are left alone.', 'Fill in from website (Operator and above): searches for and verifies the provider\'s own website when none is recorded, then reads its public contacts and finds its central pages with Firecrawl; progress is on the button and in Task manager.', 'Find scholarships now (Operator and above): maps the provider\'s site through the scraper, finds and reads every scholarship page and links courses from the evidence; progress is on the button and in Task manager.', 'Edit provider details, including the state, province or region, and "Enrols international students" (Pipeline Operator and above).'] },
  contacts: { answers: 'Who are the international recruitment contacts for each provider?', read: ['Contacts with their source and when they were last checked.'], act: ['Correct or add a contact.'] },
  scholarships: { answers: 'Which scholarships exist, and which are published?', read: ['v2.15.301: the Extraction tab moved to Models & services › AI & OpenRouter.', 'Stricter proof (v2.15.251): the quote for who a scholarship is for must itself name international (or domestic) students; a quote that is merely on the page no longer proves it. Second model confirms admissions (on by default, Scholarships › Extraction): an admission by the first model is read again by the next model, whose answer decides.', 'Model order and Layer 4 (v2.15.250): on Scholarships › Extraction, Set the order chooses the model that reads first and the one that reads next (each qualified with the current instructions). The next model reads a page again only when the first one\'s reply fails, the name is not on the page, or a fact it states is not proven by its quote. A page no model can settle goes to Layer 4 › AI could not decide, which shows every answer with its quotes and the stored copy: Admit takes the chosen answer as confirmed (the hourly publish checks still apply), Refuse needs a reason. The decision is kept: the same page copy is decided the same way later. Re-read parked scholarships with AI reads active scholarships that are not published, and held ones, again; a hold a person made stays, an automatic hold is released when the re-read passes every check. Layer 4 course items (intakes, English, fees) at universities whose adapter admits that field are closed and the course page read again by the adapter; course addresses stay with a person.', 'Extraction (v2.15.249, Scholarships › Extraction, Platform Admin): code still reads each scholarship page through the scraper and keeps a copy; a pinned AI model then reads the copy and answers with the name, who it is for, whether it is offered, the value, levels, courses and dates, each with an exact quote that is checked against the page (a fact whose quote is not on the page counts as not stated). Each model is qualified on the sample (pages a person checked, and pages marked not scholarships) and shows how often it was right; qualifying never switches anything on. Make active and Switch AI admission on are separate steps, each with a reason. While AI admission is on, new and re-read pages are admitted or refused by the AI answer and then pass the same hourly publish checks; Re-check the watch list with AI queues the watch-list universities, and the rest follow nightly. Try a page reads one address without changing anything. Changing the instructions makes a new version and switches AI admission off until the model is qualified again.', 'Find scholarships now (v2.15.248): opening the task (Task manager while it runs, Jobs after) or a university on Coverage shows the journey per university in five steps: Found (how many new pages, from the site map, a listing page or search), Read (pages and scraper credits), Decided (became a scholarship, refused with the reason in plain words, too thin to read, skipped by a rule, already held), Records (new, updated, unchanged) and Published (live, goes live at the next automatic publish at 29 minutes past each hour, or what blocks it). Every page links to its stored copy and every scholarship to its record; while a task runs it shows about how long is left. Pages that are never scholarships (short courses, research papers, help pages, alumni and staff pages) are skipped before reading by address rules under Settings and jobs, which a Platform Admin can add or switch off. A page that lists scholarships is suggested as the listing page. A scholarship published automatically that later fails a check is held at the next hourly publish and taken off search.', 'Coverage (Scholarships › Coverage): each provider measured against its own scholarship listing page. Listed = scholarships the page names; Found = those we hold; Published = those published; Missing = listed with no record of ours; Other records = ours the page does not name. State: No listing page, Reading, To check, Changed since check, Checked. Open a provider to see each listed scholarship beside our record (value, linked courses, why it is not published) and act: Publish (passes every check), Hold or Withdraw (with a reason from a short list; it stays out of automatic publishing until released), International (confirm a scholarship listed on the international page is for international students). Sign off when the list and ours agree; a change to the listing page shows Changed since check. The watch list (PIM Operator and above) is checked first. Listing pages are read weekly; add one by hand or use a suggested one (Platform Admin).', 'Automatic publishing: every hour, scholarships that pass every check are published as a batch named auto-publish; the last three days are listed at the top of Coverage for review, each with Hold. Switch it off under Coverage › Settings and jobs.', 'Course links come from the saved page, in this order: the courses it names (course code or title, never those it excludes), English language courses for an English course scholarship, then the study levels and fields it states; each link shows its proof (Show the courses and why each is linked). A page that names no course, level or field is not linked to courses and can still be published. Semester or year editions of one scholarship are held as "another edition", and the provider\'s own current record is the one listed. Wix, the website and Zoho receive published scholarships only.', 'Scholarships, their course links and their publishing state. Where they come from: each provider\'s own scholarship pages only, in every country, read through the scraper (Firecrawl, the rendered page; there is no direct read and no fallback). Each page is saved as evidence and read by fixed rules, with the page\'s own words kept. No national register or third-party directory is used (Study Australia retired 11 Oct 2026).', 'Where scholarships are set up (Decision 251): Layer 1 Register › Scholarships — the countries switched on; Layer 2 Discovery & reading › Scholarships — what was found, read, added and refused by country, scraper credits, worker answers, the per-run limits and job switches; Scholarships › Coverage — publishing (automatic every hour, or Publish, Hold or Withdraw per provider; Layer 4 › Scholarship publishing was retired on 12 Oct 2026).', 'The Scholarships list shows published scholarships only — the ones on the website and in Zoho. Ready, held and withdrawn scholarships are handled in Layers 1 and 2 and on Scholarships › Coverage (publishing). List columns: Scholarship (with its provider and how many courses it is linked to), Value, Who it is for (audience and any nationalities named, or Any nationality) and Closes. Filters: Country, Provider, Audience and Course.', 'Countries: Australian, New Zealand and Canadian universities (Decision 250). Each university\'s own scholarship pages are found and read the same way; amounts are kept in the university\'s own currency (A$, NZ$, C$) and domestic-only wording is read for that country.', 'Scholarship record: one row per fact — Who it is for, Nationalities, Value, How long, Who qualifies, Application, Provider page, Courses it applies to — each marked Read from page or Entered by hand, with the page\'s own words beneath. Change (Curator and above) saves the value as entered by hand, with a reason kept in the history; the hourly readers then leave it alone until you choose Let automation update this. Courses it applies to shows the count by study level and, under Show the courses, each linked course (opens its record). Applications open, Applications close (with any rounds) and Study start show the words on the page. Evidence & extraction shows the whole journey: the provider page, the scraper read (when, credits, next read), the saved copy (open it in Evidence), whether the page names the scholarship, every fact read with its words, what it changed (including course links) and the publishing checks.', 'Audience (who each scholarship is for) is read hourly from the scholarship\'s own name, description and criteria: International students, Domestic students, International and domestic, or Not stated on the page; the matched phrase is kept as the basis, and a value set by hand is never changed. The Audience filter on the list uses it; only International and International-and-domestic scholarships can be published (Decision 244).', 'Nationalities named on the page ("citizens of India", "students from South Asia") are read the same way, hourly, with the phrase kept; an empty list means the page names none (Decision 246). A page that states several values ("20% or 70%", "A$2,500, A$5,000 or A$15,000") gives award tiers and the value is shown as a range; a range counts as a stated value for publishing and is never used for a saving (Decision 245).', 'Scholarship record › Who qualifies and How long: who can apply (student type, new or current students, full-time, minimum ATAR, GPA or average, citizenship, automatic consideration) and how long the award runs, each with the provider page\'s own words.', 'Search by Course (title or CRICOS code) to list the scholarships linked to that course. The Value column shows the value built from what was recorded ("20% of tuition fees", "A$10,000 a year"), never page text (Decision 248).', 'Ready to publish: scholarships that pass every check are published automatically every hour (Scholarships › Coverage lists the last three days, each with Hold); a provider\'s others are published, held or withdrawn from its row on Coverage. A value shown as "Up to ..." is a maximum and is never used for a fee saving.', 'Domestic only: scholarships whose provider page names domestic students only; they are not published.', 'Course record › Scholarships: the saving a year from the provider\'s annual international tuition fee, where the scholarship is a percentage off tuition; for an Australian course with no such fee, an estimate from the registered CRICOS course cost (total ÷ years), marked as an estimate (Decision 247). The course\'s scholarships (search, website, Zoho) are the published ones linked to it, refreshed every 15 minutes and fully each night.', 'When a provider changes something: a published or ready scholarship\'s page is read again at least every 30 days. A new value, percentage, closing date or rule updates the record (never a value entered by hand) and reaches its courses within 15 minutes; savings are worked out again each morning. One that no longer passes a check (closed, no longer offered, now domestic only) is withdrawn at the daily publication review. A new scholarship found on a provider site is published automatically when it passes every check, or waits as held on Scholarships › Coverage until a Platform Admin publishes it.', 'Zoho and the website receive a course\'s published scholarships through the course API (action "scholarships"): value and tiers, who it is for, nationalities, who qualifies in the page\'s words, saving per year (marked when estimated), dates and the page link.'], act: ['Run it now (Operator and above; each starts a task shown on the button and in Scheduled jobs › Task manager): Find scholarships now on a provider record or on Scholarships › Coverage (one provider, or tick up to 50) maps the site through the scraper, screens candidate pages, admits new scholarships, reads every scholarship page and links courses by the evidence rules; Check scholarships for this course on a course record reads the provider\'s scholarship pages again and lists the scholarships added to or removed from the course; Read again now on a scholarship record reads its page again. About one scraper credit a page. A task for the same target cannot be started twice; Cancel stops it.', 'Which courses a scholarship applies to comes from the study levels, fields and courses its own page names, rebuilt each time the page is read (Layer 2); there is no separate Course links screen (retired 4 Oct 2026).', 'Publish, hold or withdraw on Scholarships › Coverage (Platform Admin).', 'Before publishing, open a few ready records and compare the eligibility shown with the provider page; a wrong reading is fixed on the record, not by publishing.', 'Domestic only: open the page; when international students can apply, choose International students can apply and note what the page says (Platform Admin).'] },
  entry: { answers: 'What academic entry requirement does each provider and course publish for a student\'s country of prior education, where did it come from, and what does the website return?', read: ['v2.15.366: countries are offered India, Nepal, Singapore first, then A to Z; a level label naming several levels ("Diploma/Associate degrees") counts for each; New Zealand courses with an approved strong identity proof can be read at course level.', 'v2.15.364: Course entry requirements has a Course-level reading panel: by provider, the courses that can be read, read, waiting in Layer 4, admitted, with no row kept and remaining, with the estimated cost; a Platform Admin previews and asks for the next bounded batch with a reason. Sources, reads and holds shows a rendered page with no requirements table as a Layer 4 note, and as No matrix published (confirmed) once approved. Read again on a markdown-stored page fetches it again as HTML.', 'v2.15.363 (AER operations workspace): four views. Provider entry matrix: one row per country, level and qualification, with band, minimum, scale, quote and status. Course entry requirements: what a course\'s own page asks for. Sources, reads and holds: each official page or PDF, its stored copy, its latest read and why rows were held or not kept. Resolution inspection: which of the five rules gives a course\'s requirement for a country, and why the earlier rules did not.', 'The summary above each view: Active (reaches the website), Waiting in Layer 4 (read by AI, not approved), Quarantined (evidence in doubt), Withdrawn or superseded, Sources held, Courses with requirements.', 'Only active rows reach the website and Zoho. A waiting row is decided in Layer 4, never here.', 'Open a row for its full quote, source, stored copy, reading run, Layer 4 item and the history of every change by a person.'], act: ['Curator and above: Edit in list to correct an active or quarantined row; give the reason first. A value not printed in the quote is refused; a row changed by someone else since you opened it is refused (reload and try again).', 'Add requirement from the provider\'s own source and its stored copy; Withdraw, Quarantine or Restore with a reason.', 'Platform Admin: Read again on one source (Sources, reads and holds) with a reason; a source held as unreadable waits for a reader change.', 'Use Resolution inspection to check what a course returns for a country before answering a question about it.'] },
  rankings: { answers: 'How does each university rank, and how do providers compare?', read: ['QS and THE: filter by country, state, provider and whether a university is linked to a provider.', 'A linked provider name opens its provider record.', 'Compare, QILT outcomes and PRISMS student flow tabs.', 'Datasets (v2.15.301): Ranking imports (was Reference data › Ranking imports) is below the dataset list, Pipeline Operator and above.'], act: ['Link a ranked university with no provider (Curator and above): pick a suggestion or search; the link covers every edition.', 'Universities are linked automatically every hour when the names agree in the same country; close matches wait for a person.'] },
  reference: { answers: 'Which dates and outside sites does the platform use?', read: ['v2.15.301 (Platform Admin, 20 Oct 2026, "One list with a type filter"): Key dates and Reference sources are one list; the type filter shows All, Key dates or Reference sources. Ranking imports moved to Rankings & statistics › Datasets.', 'Ranking imports, key dates and reference sources. Reference sources (v2.15.246) is a list with expandable rows: the filters (site, uses, category, country, status) line up with the columns; open a row to see its purpose and to edit it with the same fields as Add site (changing domain, uses, category or country needs a reason).'], act: ['Import a new ranking edition; add a key date; register a reference source.'] },
  coverage: { answers: 'How complete is the catalogue, and how is the platform progressing?', read: ['v2.15.305 (Platform Admin, 21 Oct 2026 "Keep two, fix reader"): delivery modes. Blended means every student mixes campus and online study inside one course (hours or a share each way, or online with block weeks on campus); On campus or online means the page offers a choice of modes; online offered to domestic students only is read as on campus. Course pages use the words both ways, so the reader now tells a list of options from a mix. Attributes › Delivery wording: a university\'s own phrase and the mode it means (UNSW "Face-to-face (includes blended)" is on campus), added or switched off by a PIM Admin or above with a reason; each change re-runs the cross-check. Held values are not changed: the Cross-check differences list shows where the held mode and the page differ.', 'v2.15.304 (Platform Admin, 21 Oct 2026: "Field Stalled and action to resolve it"; the 10-minute check): Attributes opens on Stalled fields: every field below its target that has gained less than 1 point in 7 days (Not moving), trails the best country by 30 points or more (Behind other countries), or has no reader yet; with its main cause (pages read do not state it, pages not read yet, no course page, waiting for a person, being filled), the action that resolves it and the five universities missing it most. Fill now (Pipeline Operator) starts an Enrich fields task for that field and country; Release holds and fill (Platform Admin, with a reason) first releases the "page did not state it" holds, for use after a new central page, adapter rule or reader. Platform health raises the same list every 3 hours (one issue per country, one for fields with no reader, one when Fill the gaps has not run for 7 hours) and closes an issue when the field moves. The periods and points are on Settings › Pipeline settings › Re-read and retry. The 10-minute check (weekly): 1 Stalled fields: act on each Not moving row (Fill now, adapter work for the listed universities, or a lower target with a reason); 2 Every field by country: read across each row for a country far behind; 3 Filled by: No reader yet is a build task; 4 Fill the gaps: a recent run and values filled in 7 days; 5 Cross-check differences: many on one field means a reading rule to fix; 6 Platform health: no open field_stalled warning older than a week.', 'v2.15.303 (Platform Admin, 21 Oct 2026: "all data fields ... not the top 7"; "same attributes completeness across the board"): Attributes opens on Every field by country: 15 course fields and 9 provider fields, each with how it is filled and its target (80%; the Platform Admin changes a target with a reason); a share below target is marked. Fill the gaps (standing queue): every 6 hours, when the previous run has finished, one Enrich fields task takes every missing field that is due (stored pages and adapter readings first, then the AI, then up to 200 new page reads a day); a field the page did not state is tried again when the page is read again with new content, or after 60 days (Settings › Pipeline settings › Re-read and retry); Check now (Pipeline Operator) and Switch on or off with a reason (Platform Admin). Cross-check differences: a held duration, study level or delivery mode that differs from the latest page reading, with the page words; Keep held, or Take page value (locked as entered by hand). The attribute table below now lists every course field, with In the fill queue and No reader yet.', 'v2.15.301 (Platform Admin, 20 Oct 2026): Progress keeps two views, Overview and Journeys. Running now is Scheduled jobs › Task manager (and Layer 2/3 › Operations by stage); Levers retired, the pace settings are on Settings. Flags moved to Layer 2/3 › Flags.', 'Progress tab (v2.15.266): how the platform is progressing, what is running and where to tweak it, in four views. Overview: pick all universities, the pilot or the top 50 Australian; Needs attention (stopped universities by reason, Firecrawl and AI notices), where the universities are in the seven-stage journey (each stage opens Journeys), courses with intakes, English, fee and delivery (when picked → now for a group), scholarships found and published, course pages read in the last hour, Firecrawl and AI today, and every hour of the last 24 (snapshots kept 90 days). Journeys (v2.15.267, as the approved mock-up): filters for group, country, stage, what holds a university up and Only held up; rows sorted by courses with the adapter journey as seven stage pills, fields filled, the scholarship journey (found, with the AI, published), Held up by and a Next step button; a row opens its steps (each stage with its time and note) and the run-on-demand actions for that university: Find scholarships now, read its scholarship pages with AI again, read its course pages again, Qualify adapter, Retry onboarding and Search again. Running now: every scheduled job by journey stage, Running, Waiting, Failing or Paused, its last result, Pause, Resume and Run now (Platform Admin), and Workers sending back errors (Mark as seen (Pipeline Operator and above) hides one that is understood); a job opens to the universities it worked on in the last hour, or, when it touched none, the universities now at its stage of the journey, each linking to its journey; schedules are shown in words. Levers: every setting that changes the pace (onboarding, Firecrawl budget, AI guards) with its value and what it did today, linking to where it is changed; and the run-on-demand actions.', 'The Universities tab is retired: each university\'s adapter, coverage and indicative whole-course fees are now in its row under Layer 2 › Adapters, where the same fees (lowest and highest, in the country\'s currency: current fees first, the CRICOS registered total as the fallback, award courses only). A range is shown outside the admin screens only once a Platform Admin publishes it for that university, and a range set by hand is never changed. Hosted courses: an award inside or at the exit of a longer course takes its values from its single-degree parent once the register check passes, a page carrying several courses hosts them when host pages are admitted, and double degrees or pages that are gone wait for a Platform Admin.', 'Courses tab: courses with an official page, English requirements, intakes and a current fee. It opens on all countries; choose a country or type a university to narrow every count. Layer 1 values come from each country\'s register (CRICOS, NZQA).', 'Link refresh: how often each kind of course link is checked again, and which portals supply links.', 'Attributes tab: opens with the 80% target panel. Intakes, English and fees are each measured on their own against 80% of active courses, with who supplied each value (adapter, central page, page reader, entered by hand or other) and how many more courses each field needs. Below it, the same by attribute. Fee schedules, English policies and academic calendars are approved in Layer 2 › Adapter builder (1.3) or on Layer 2 › Onboarding.', 'The course drawer\'s Fees section starts with Fee used (Rule 2, 8 Oct 2026): the fee on the provider\'s own course page whenever its evidence is captured, whatever year it names, with no review; otherwise the CRICOS registered fee divided by the course length (held until a page fee with evidence arrives), with the reason. A page on a site shared by several providers does not count, and a fee entered or locked by hand keeps the earlier rule. Nothing stored changes. The same fee_used is returned by the Zoho, Wix and website course APIs. Fees on pages that switch between a domestic and an international view ("This content is for domestic students", "Switch to International") follow the view they sit in. A course total or a fee for one study period, trimester or unit is never taken as an annual fee.', 'How a course page is accepted as the course\'s own: Australia, the CRICOS code printed on the page or the exact course title as the heading. New Zealand, the course\'s programme code or a labelled NZQA number on the page, the exact title, or the NZQA title without "(Level N)" as the heading with the same level shown on the page. A page naming the same qualification at another level is not accepted on its title. NZ fees are read in NZ dollars and, as in Australia, are taken only from a page that prints the course\'s code, then checked by the tested AI model before they are added. Australian English is also taken from a page whose title is exactly the course title. New Zealand degrees (bachelor to doctor) are also accepted when the heading is exactly the degree name, optionally followed by its abbreviation, and the page names no other level of it. Canada: each university\'s own site is found by name and accepted only on its own .ca site whose home page names it (in the title, the heading, or anywhere on the page when the address fits the name) or prints its DLI number; a course page is accepted on the exact course title, or when its heading names the same field and the same award (not a combined or dual award, not another campus, not an archived calendar page). Canadian fees are read in Canadian dollars and taken only from a page that prints the course\'s code; Canadian courses carry no official code yet, so none are added until one exists.'], act: ['Change a link refresh schedule or switch a portal on (Pipeline Operator and above).'] },
  layer1: { answers: 'Are the official registers (CRICOS, NZQA) loaded and current, and is every other source the pipeline reads healthy?', read: ['v2.15.301 (Platform Admin, 20 Oct 2026, "Merge into one Sources page"): one Sources page with a layer filter. Registers (Layer 1), the default, is the list below with run, schedule and settings; All layers lists every source the pipeline reads, across all layers, with its health and history (the old Sources page, whose address opens this filter). Layer 1 › Scholarships moved to Layer 2/3 › Scholarships.', 'Sources (v2.15.246): one list of every register, statistics file and ranking, filtered by source, country, type and health. Each row shows pills for its country, type, health, last run and schedule; one that needs attention says why (for example a check that expected 195 records and got 200). Open a row to see its facts, the run in progress, links to its jobs and evidence, and its settings (address, authority, format, schedule, how often it is checked and loaded, and the record-change limits), which a Platform Admin edits in place with a reason. Run now, Check source and Pause or Resume are on the row. + Add source records a new register, paused until a reader is assigned. A source is rerun when it is due and its file has changed; a source whose file changes on every read but whose last two runs changed nothing waits for its next due date. Manual batch runs and the separate Source settings page are retired.', 'Scholarships: countries switched on for scholarships (amounts kept in each country\'s currency) and every scholarship source by country — Ingest (read into records, with how often the feed is read), University pages, Reference (for looking up) and Validation (to compare with our records). A Platform Admin adds a source, changes its use, pauses it or changes how often a feed is read, always with a reason. A source added for Ingest stays Registered until a reader exists for it.'], act: ['Start or re-run a register load (Pipeline Operator; settings Platform Admin).', 'Pause or re-check a source.'] },
  layer2: { answers: 'Where is each university in finding its pages, building and admitting its adapter, enriching its courses and checking its scholarships, and what is stopped?', read: ['v2.15.312 (Platform Admin, 22 Oct 2026): unpublished providers are left out of every scheduled job and come back when published again; what a person starts still runs. Every published provider with its own website and no adapter is in onboarding, which finds its course pages and builds its adapter. On Providers, filter by Adapter and sort the Adapter column.', 'v2.15.310 (Platform Admin, 22 Oct 2026): on Flags, each held university or course says what was tried before it was flagged: the site map (pages listed and course-like pages), course-page search, page reads, AI page match and AI field reader, each with times used, worked and did not work, credits and AI cost (History shows the same as a table). A university whose own site lists too few course pages is held as Search off: the site lists too few course pages; add its pages by hand or Search again.', 'v2.15.309 (Platform Admin, 21 Oct 2026 20:02, AI fee reader): Layer 2/3 › Enrich fields › Fee reader (AI). The platform reads each provider\'s fee pages with its AI model into rows as published, works out a yearly figure (estimated from a fee per credit, point or term with the country\'s full-time load) and matches each row to a course. Rows matched surely enough are admitted; the rest go to Layer 4. Every mistake (rows with no course, a different currency, an amount far from the country\'s usual fees, rows a person rejected, a page that changed) is kept and given to the AI on the next read with the provider\'s reading notes. Scope (countries and provider types) and limits are on Settings › Pipeline settings › Enrichment; a new country is a row in Country rules.', 'v2.15.308 (Platform Admin, 21 Oct 2026 18:36, "Two tracks + more credits"): in each enrichment plan, Fill missing fields (stored pages and AI) runs on its own track beside the website, course-page, adapter and scholarship steps, so it no longer waits for an adapter. Automatic plans take the countries in Automatic enrichment plans: countries first (Settings › Pipeline settings › Onboarding; New Zealand) first. The daily Firecrawl budget and shares and the plans started an hour were raised; they are on Models & services › Toolsets & limits and Settings › Pipeline settings.', 'v2.15.307 (Platform Admin, 21 Oct 2026 17:30): tasks an enrichment plan starts show "Enrichment plan (automatic)" or "Enrichment plan (Run now)" under Started by in Task manager. A plan that finishes with a step that did not get through (the adapter built but no field passed its check, too few course pages, a failed or skipped step) or with an adapter ready to admit is listed under Plans that need a person, with what to do. Search refreshes asked for only by Enrich fields tasks and plans run at most every Search refresh for automatic changes (Settings › Pipeline settings › Website API).', 'v2.15.306 (Platform Admin, 21 Oct 2026: "end to end data enrichment for universities ... automation is gated by toolset configurable limits but manual should decide on screen of required toolset usage"): Enrichment plan tab, and Plan on each university row. A university\'s plan comes from its own gaps, in order: 1 website, contacts and central pages; 2 find course pages; 3 build the adapter (onboarding; retried when stopped); 4 admit (a person); 5 fill missing fields (Enrich fields, AI on, new reads allowed; fields already tried on the same page are left out); 6 find and read scholarships. Each step shows why, the fields it fills and its estimate in Firecrawl credits and AI US$, from what the same step used in the last 30 days. Run now (Pipeline Operator, with a reason) runs the ticked steps in order from the on-demand allowance (Firecrawl credits and AI a day, set on Models & services › Toolsets & limits): the daily shares and per-university caps do not apply to it, a directory site is still never paid for, and Run now is refused when the estimate is more than what is left. Automatic plans (switched on and off by the Platform Admin with a reason) start hourly for the universities with the most missing values, 10 an hour and 20 open at once; each automatic step waits for room in its toolset share and is skipped after 48 hours. Each run records what it used and the fields gained. Limits: Settings › Pipeline settings › Onboarding (plans.*).', 'Layer 2/3 Build & enrich (v2.15.300, Platform Admin 20 Oct 2026: one operations area). Operations (first tab): each stage (find the website, find course pages, build the adapter, admit and enrich, scholarships) with the universities working on it now, waiting for it, and stopped for a person (each kind opens Layer 4 › Inbox on that kind), and the scheduled jobs behind it (Pause, Resume and Run now, Platform Admin); the onboarding pace, Onboard universities not yet queued, the onboarding settings, and the central pages waiting for approval across universities. Universities: one row per university with an adapter, in the Firecrawl targets or in onboarding, showing its journey stage, why it stopped and how many Inbox items it has; open a row for its onboarding (what to do, Retry or Stop with a reason, and the journey), its adapter, schedule, central pages, fees, hosted courses and courses; Builder opens the Adapter builder for that university. The Onboarding and Adapters tabs, the How an adapter goes live and What each university needs next cards and the page-fee dry run are retired; their addresses open Universities. ', 'Firecrawl daily budget (v2.15.262; Models & services › Firecrawl › Daily budget, Platform Admin with a reason): Firecrawl may bill up to 15,000 credits a Melbourne day, shared by purpose: finding course pages 6,000, reading pages Firecrawl must read 3,000, scholarships 3,500, central pages 1,500, other 1,000. A purpose that has used its share waits until midnight. Per university: scholarship work stops at 150 credits in 30 days, central pages are read again only after 30 days, and course-page search stops after 30 searches with no correct page (listed as Search stopped; check the website, then Search again). Firecrawl credits by university (same page) shows, for the last hour, 24 hours or 7 days, each university\'s credits by purpose against the course pages produced (correct, and wrong pages Firecrawl read) and credits per correct page, with a flag where credits are wasted. A notice appears at 80% of a share or of the day.', 'Top 50 Australian providers (cohort au-top-2026-10-12, 12 Oct 2026): the 50 Australian providers with the most CRICOS courses are onboarded first, largest first; small pilot members not yet started are held at the back of the queue.', 'Course pages (v2.15.261): each course\'s page is found by Firecrawl search (CRICOS code, then title). A page the search found is read directly first; Firecrawl (basic proxy) reads it only when the direct read is blocked or the page needs a browser, to save Firecrawl credits, and since v2.15.263 only when the page was found by its CRICOS code, is listed on the university\'s own site or was entered by a person (pages found by a title or web search are read directly only: Firecrawl read the right page for 99.7% of CRICOS-code finds but under half of title-search finds). One reader runs every 30 seconds, up to 20 pages a university (the second reader is paused on Scheduled jobs › Automations). Onboarding keeps moving: a university whose search is finished and that has had no page read for an hour stops as Too few course pages, so the next university starts, and carries on by itself once enough of its pages are read; AI allowance used carries on by itself when the allowance renews; a missing website stops as No website and carries on once one is entered.', 'Admit automatically (Layer 2 › Onboarding settings, v2.15.259; Platform Admin, with a reason; switched on 12 Oct 2026): a university at Ready to admit has exactly the fields that passed the admit rule admitted by itself (within 10 minutes), logged with the reason, and the row and its journey say "Admitted automatically" with the fields. It then goes on to Enrich courses, Scholarship adapter and Admit scholarships. A field that did not pass is never admitted, and Needs a person still needs a person. Undo for one university: Layer 2 › Adapters, Admit off (with a reason). Switching the setting off stops new automatic admits.', 'Pilot (Layer 2 › Onboarding, v2.15.259): a group of universities (60 Australian, 25 New Zealand, 15 Canadian on 12 Oct 2026) measured hourly by the onboarding-pilot-snapshot job. For each country: universities at each stage, needs a person or stopped, admitted automatically, the share of active courses with intakes, English, fee and delivery when picked and now, and scholarships published when picked and now; AI cost since picked. Refresh now reads it live; Show pilot only filters the list.', 'Onboarding (Layer 2 › Onboarding, v2.15.258; Curator and above to view, Platform Admin to act): every university goes through seven stages, shown as a strip of counts (press one to show those rows) and as a stepper on each row. 1 Provider in: it is in the platform from a Layer 1 register, another database or our search, and queued. 2 Prepare: website, contacts, central pages and course pages found and read. 3 Create adapter: the pinned AI proposes the settings from sample pages; saved in testing, applied and qualified. 4 Admit: a Platform Admin admits the passing fields on Layer 2 › Adapters (or approves central pages when nothing passes). 5 Enrich courses: the admitted adapter writes its values to the courses; the stage ends when no value has changed for 10 minutes and records what was written. 6 Scholarship adapter: the scholarship search starts only now. 7 Admit scholarships: the AI reads and checks each page; held pages wait for a person; Done when none waits (or after 7 days). Up to 100 universities are worked at once; universities waiting at Admit, Enrich or Admit scholarships do not count towards that. The pace (universities that finished a stage in the last hour and 6 hours) and an estimate for the queue are shown. Onboard universities not yet queued adds only universities without an admitting adapter that are not already in onboarding; it is greyed out when every one is queued.', 'Intakes, English requirements and fees are read by university adapters (Layer 2 › Adapters) and admitted from them; there is no separate AI check (Layer 3 was retired on 12 Oct 2026). A university without an adapter uses its university-wide academic calendar and English policy defaults.', 'Adapter builder (PIM Admin and above; saving and admitting are Platform Admin): one numbered page (v2.15.245). 1 Provider: find any provider. 1.1 Website: where it came from (found by search and verified by its CRICOS code, DLI number or its name on its home page, or entered by hand). Every provider without one is searched automatically, in every country, and a verified website goes on the record by itself (never over one entered by hand); Fill in from website runs it now as a task, or enter it by hand. Everything after depends on it. 1.2 Contacts: public phone and email read from the site. 1.3 Central pages: key dates, the international fee schedule and English requirements; Firecrawl maps the site and suggests the likeliest pages (marked found by Firecrawl), and you attach the right one; attached pages are read and wait for approval right there in 1.3, with this university\'s fee schedules, English policies and academic calendars and Approve or Reject on each (since 12 Oct 2026; Layer 4 › Attributes was retired). 2 Course pages. 2.1 Find course pages: every course from the register with its page (read, stored, searching, not found on the site, no page yet); Find with Firecrawl searches the provider\'s site for the ticked or all missing pages as a task, or enter a page by hand. 2.2 Capture sample pages: 6 spread across course types (about 1 credit each); add any course as a sample. 3 Adapter. 3.1 The model proposes the settings (a Platform Admin can choose the model for this adapter); an answer cut off at its length limit is asked again once, automatically, with a larger limit, and the tokens and cost of each attempt are shown. 3.2 Save in testing and apply. 3.3 Qualify. 3.4 Admit the ready fields (pass the admit rule and agree with held values: 90% or more on 3 or more courses, read on 5 or more pages). 4 Adjust by hand (collapsed): mark text blocks or page-data values, preview, save, validate and admit by field. Nothing runs on a schedule except the searches, and a passing check never admits by itself. Platform Admins also see an Adapter column on the Providers list: Open adapter or Create adapter opens this tab with the provider loaded.', 'Adapters (the opening tab; Pipeline Operators see it read only, Qualify needs PIM Admin, and Admit or switching needs Platform Admin): one collapsed row per university with its test, Qualify and Admit, on/off switch (with what switching off does stated), read schedule (7 to 365 days, default 90; a changed page makes new evidence, an unchanged page does not), central pages, fee range and rules, Read pages again, hosted courses, Firecrawl target and history. Bulk Qualify and Admit work on the filtered list. Below the list: Firecrawl runs and targets (credits left are on Models & services), Page fees against CRICOS (dry run), which shows what a page-fee-wins rule would change, read only, and the fee range and award link settings. An adapter\'s raw settings text (JSON) is under Advanced (Platform Admin). Admit is a separate, deliberate step and values entered by hand are never changed. Overview, Fetch an area, History and Source profiles are retired.', 'Scholarships: by country — universities searched, pages found and read, pages added as scholarships or refused (with the commonest reasons), and re-reads of known pages; worker answers for the last 6 hours; the per-run limits (universities per run, pages read per run, queue size, re-read interval) and the jobs, which a Platform Admin can change or pause with a reason. Firecrawl credits for scholarships shows credits used and left; the cap is a setting here. Every scholarship page, listing page, discovery candidate and site map is read through the scraper (Platform Admin, 11 Oct 2026): no direct read, no fallback, robots.txt not consulted for scholarship pages. A page waits when the scraper cannot be used (cap reached or service unavailable) and is tried again within the hour.', 'Fetch an area: choose a country, state or university to see where it stands in the course-page sweep (sites mapped or not found, pages found and read, facts admitted) with a one-line reading of what is holding it up. Start (Pipeline Operator and above) puts it first in the sweep: it searches again for sites not found, retries failed site maps, searches for pages of courses with none (a search that found nothing is repeated after 7 days) and reads found pages now. Nothing admitted or entered by hand is changed.', 'Overview › Action required lists only Layer 2 jobs that are failing or stuck and workers sending back errors, each with what it means, what to do, and a button to Live activity or Scheduled jobs. When nothing needs action it says so.', 'History › Daily progress: for one country, the courses with an official page, English, intakes and tuition admitted on each day, with the change from the day before. The execution trace follows.', 'Course-page search, page reading and the fee schedule reader run as automations (Scheduled jobs). The older provider-reading pipeline (waves, fan-out and qualification batches) was switched off on 2 Oct 2026 and its jobs, screens and workers were removed on 9 Oct 2026; its history is kept.', 'Flags (v2.15.301, moved from Coverage & completeness): what is held out of the queues, why, and its history; release or hold.', 'Scholarships (v2.15.301, one tab): Finding scholarships (countries switched on and their sources, was Layer 1 › Scholarships), then Reading scholarships (discovery and reading by country, refusals, jobs and limits).'], act: ['Open a provider\'s adapter on Adapters to test, qualify or admit it, or switch it on or off.', 'Add a new provider, or fix one whose pages are not read, with the guided Adapter builder.'] },
  layer4: { answers: 'What needs a person\'s judgement?', read: ['v2.15.300 (Platform Admin, 20 Oct 2026): the Review queue, AI could not decide and Websites to find tabs and Coverage › Counsellor reports retired. Everything that needs a person is in the Inbox, by university or by kind: course links, held scholarships (with the AI re-check), websites needed, counsellor reports (closed here as Fixed or Not changed; Zoho shows the outcome) and providers that left the register (closed, merged with a successor named by name or code, or still operating). Decided lists the decisions taken here with who, when and why. The old addresses open the Inbox on their kind. ', 'Layer 4 is where decisions that need a person wait: the review queue, AI could not decide (scholarship pages no model could settle) and Websites to find. Every decision is kept with who made it and when.', 'Retired on 12 Oct 2026 (v2.15.253): Flagged values, Fee rules, Attributes, Scholarship publishing and Blocks. The open flagged fees were closed (the fees are kept and each university\'s adapter reads them again); fee rule results are kept. Central page approvals (fee schedules, English policies, academic calendars) moved to Layer 2 › Adapter builder (1.3) and Layer 2 › Onboarding › Approvals waiting; scholarships are published from Scholarships › Coverage; blocks already recorded stay in force. Old addresses open the new places (Flagged values, Fee rules and Blocks open the Review queue).', 'Tuition: where the regulator publishes it (Australia: CRICOS gives each course\'s international course cost), that is the tuition shown, and provider pages are not searched for a fee; provider-page tuition is read only where the regulator publishes none (New Zealand, Canada), for international students. ' + 'Tuition reviews are settled against the page\'s international view every 10 minutes: when the amount asked about is not the international annual fee (a domestic price, a loan cap, a bursary, a whole-course total), the review is closed with both amounts kept; reviews whose amount is the page\'s international fee, or whose page shows only per-session fees and course totals, stay for a person.', 'Websites to find lists universities whose own website the finder could not confirm, with the search and the pages it tried. Enter the official website and Save (Curator and above): it is kept as entered by a person, the site is mapped and the course-page search starts.'], act: ['Approve, correct or reject, with a reason. Oldest first.', 'Websites to find (Curator and above): enter the official website and Save.'] },
  health: { answers: 'Is anything broken or about to run out, and which screens are not used?', read: ['v2.15.301 (Platform Admin, 20 Oct 2026): Capacity moved to the Go-live checklist. Storage & retention (Platform Admin, was its own page) is the second tab, as described below.', 'Storage sizes (v2.15.286), first on the page: recorded every day at about 00:25 Melbourne time. Tiles for the database, file storage (all buckets) and tables; By day (database and file storage for the last 30 days); Buckets (files, size, change in 7 days); Schemas; Tables (size split into table, indexes and long values, estimated rows, change in 1 and 7 days; the largest 25, or tick All, with a filter). Measure now (Platform Admin) records today again. Table rows are kept 365 days (setting storage.size_keep_days); daily totals are kept always.', 'Platform Admin only. The database size, then one row per category: what it holds, the rule for what would go, the size now and how much would go, when it was measured, and the last or current run. Categories: adapter builder screenshots older than 7 days (the page HTML proposals use is kept), the Layer 2 tables retired on 2 Oct 2026 (run items stay; earlier Layer 3 records point to them), the scheduled-job run log older than 7 days, and sitemap copies of third-party course directories (addresses bound to a course stay). Evidence: Run audit first; then Unreferenced evidence removes records and files the finished audit found referenced nowhere, created before it and more than 7 days ago, checking each batch again just before removal (evidence kept 365 days by policy, ranking source files and shared files are never removed).', 'Screen use (Platform Admin, v2.15.300): every page and tab of the menu with its opens, people and days used over the last 14 days (setting usage.screen_window_days); those not opened are listed first as candidates to retire. Counting started on 20 Oct 2026. ', 'Needs attention: Critical, Warning and Info.', 'Checks table, including budgets: Firecrawl balance (as Firecrawl reports it) and OpenRouter spend against the AI task limits.', 'Queues count only work a reader can take; work held on purpose (a university past its scholarship cap, small Australian providers that scholarship searches skip) is shown as held, not stalled. A job the flag unit has paused and switched on again for a trial run is not counted as overdue.'], act: ['Critical: act today. Warning: act this week or record why not.', 'Preview shows the counts and changes nothing. Purge asks for a reason and the category name typed in full; it runs in the background in small batches, can be stopped, and every run is listed under Runs. Run audit counts evidence not referenced by any value, decision or record and deletes nothing.'] },
  jobs: { answers: 'Is every automation running, and where is each long-running admin task up to?', read: ['Task manager (v2.15.285): Tasks started by people (waiting, running or paused, with pause, resume and cancel), then Background jobs: every scheduled job and worker using the platform — running this moment, failing in the last 24 hours, paused, Firecrawl credits in the last hour — with Pause, Resume and Run now; the same board is on Coverage & completeness › Progress › Running now. From v2.15.266 to v2.15.284 the background board was only on Progress. Before that, Task manager › Running now and the last 15 minutes (v2.15.246): everything using resources — totals (running now, scheduled jobs that ran, database time used, failed runs, worker and API calls, scraper credits); scheduled jobs running this minute; every scheduled job that ran in the last 15 minutes with its runs, failures, average and longest time, with Pause, Resume and Run now; worker and API calls by kind; AI model calls and their cost; scraper credits; and the work waiting in each queue with the job that works it. A scheduled job missing from the Automations catalogue is flagged. If the board cannot be read it says so instead of showing nothing.', 'Starting a task (Find scholarships now, Fill in from website, Qualify, Read pages again and the rest) asks only to confirm (v2.15.247); the log records the screen it was started from. Admit the passing fields, pause and cancel still ask for a reason. After you start one, the button or the ticked rows show its progress, and anything that stops it from starting is shown next to the button.', 'Jobs: a Layer 1 register run is one row (Register run, with what it found against the last applied register), not one row per batch; open it to see why it ran, its counts, every batch and links to the stored source files.', 'Every background feature is registered as a task type or a scheduled job and appears here with its controls (Platform Admin, 11 Oct 2026).', 'Task manager: a list only of the tasks that are waiting, running or paused right now (Qualify adapters, Read pages again, a Firecrawl run, an adapter Apply, a central page read, Find scholarships now, Check scholarships for a course, Read a scholarship again), with progress, who started it and why. Progress comes from the database, so refreshing the page loses nothing. Finished tasks are in the Jobs tab: open one to see each provider\'s result and what the task did.', 'Top cards: running, paused, runs and failures in 24 hours.', 'Each automation: what it does, how often, last run and its reason when it failed.', 'Scholarships area (all reading through the scraper): find pages (every 10 minutes), read pages (every 5 minutes), listing pages (every 15 minutes), audience and nationality from wording (hourly), automatic publishing (hourly), course scholarship list (every 15 minutes, full each morning), re-read of published ones, publication review and savings each morning (times on Scheduled jobs, in Melbourne time). The register feeds, scope rules, AI-run scheduler, country watch and weekly clean-up were retired on 11 Oct 2026. Times are Melbourne time.'], act: ['Layer 2 › Adapters › Qualify (Operator (adapters) and above): measure the chosen adapters against the admission rules; nothing is admitted. Admit the passing fields (Platform Admin) is the separate, deliberate step. Task manager: pause, resume or cancel a task; it stops at the next provider, never half way through one. Scholarship tasks can be cancelled (pages already read keep their results; the rest go back to their normal turn). A scheduled job running now can be paused (the run in progress finishes), resumed or run now from Running now (Pipeline Operator and above).', 'Pause, resume, run now, change how often and how many per run (Pipeline Operator and above).', 'Models & services › Toolsets & limits › Course-page search budget (the first panel; was on Priority queue until v2.15.300): this month\'s search credits and the monthly cap; when the cap is reached searches wait. A Platform Admin can raise the cap there.'] },
  evidence: { answers: 'Which saved page or file supports a value?', read: ['Saved source pages and files, and what they changed.', 'Open a row for its panel (v2.15.293), one screen: the course and university, the page address, when and how it was read, whether it was accepted as the course\'s page (and how) and is in use now or was replaced by a newer copy, what the page supplied, open review items and earlier or later copies. View page and Download open the saved file; Technical details (closed) has the hash, file, storage path and job.','Each row says what it is (v2.15.294): copies of a course page are numbered with the one in use marked, an older copy whose values are still in use says so, and a provider\'s facts page or a register file is named. View page opens the saved page here, as it was read.','Links from saved pages to the records they support are added every 10 minutes by Index evidence links; its progress is on Live activity.'], act: ['Open the evidence behind any value.'] },
  environment: { answers: 'What is the pipeline allowed to do, how fast, and at what cost?', read: ['v2.15.310 (Platform Admin, 22 Oct 2026): Settings › Backup & restore (Platform Admin only). Every morning at about 6:50 a backup keeps each provider\'s Published switch and every setting value (kept for the days in Storage & retention). Pick a backup to see what differs now, who changed it last and when; Download SQL file keeps a copy outside the platform. Each backup has Compare and Restore (v2.15.311); under the comparison, Restore this backup puts everything back, or tick rows and Put back chosen, with a reason: a backup of the current state is taken first, each provider change is logged, and an archived provider is never published.', 'v2.15.301: two tabs. Settings (Platform Admin): everything below. API usage (Pipeline Operator and above; was its own page, "Move API usage to Settings"): the console for the API version URLs, as described next.', 'Every call to an API version URL is logged: zoho-api-v2 (one key for the Zoho Creator app, one for the Zoho CRM sync) and website-api-v2 (one key for the website developer). Calls to the older URLs (Zoho v1, and the website through wix-course-api) are not on this page.', 'Statistics as of: the statistics refresh every day at about 00:20 Melbourne time; press Refresh statistics now for fresh figures. Period: 24 hours, 7 days or 30 days.', 'Each API: calls, success rate, failures, bandwidth sent and the last call. Keys: who uses each key, on or off, last call and last success (the last time the consumer used the API), calls, success, failures (client errors, rate limited, server errors), bandwidth, average and largest reply, times, and when it was last rotated. During a rotation overlap the old key shows until when it works and when it was last used.', 'Full loads and deltas: the last completed full load (when, how long, pages, items, load size), deltas (count, items, size, last), CSV exports and searches.', 'By day and By key and action: daily totals with bandwidth and times. Latest errors: the last 20 failed calls with their request id (quote it when the caller reports a problem). Key changes: every rotation and switch, by whom.', 'Every setting in one place, by pipeline step: universities per matcher run, matcher and search speed, pages read per batch, which page proofs admit each attribute per country, the Firecrawl limit and reserve.', 'Keys for outside services (never shown) and usage against budgets.'], act: ['Backup & restore (Platform Admin): Back up now before a large change; to undo a mistake, Compare the last daily backup, tick the rows and Put back chosen with a reason.', 'Change a number and Save (Platform Admin): it applies at once and is logged under Recent changes.', 'Tick or untick a page proof per country and attribute (Platform Admin): the identity rule changes at once; the decisions behind it stay on the row.', 'Rotate a key (Platform Admin). Never paste keys into notes or tickets.', 'Rotate (Platform Admin): makes a new key and shows it once (copy it and send it by a secure channel; it is not stored). The old key keeps working for the overlap you choose (default in Settings, API key rotation; 0 stops it at once); End old key stops it early.', 'Switch off / Switch on (Platform Admin): the key gets 401 while off.', 'Change the calls-a-minute limits, page sizes, logo link validity, Zoho change stream countries and how long single calls are kept on Settings (sections Zoho API and Website API).'] },
  services: { answers: 'Which AI models and page services are switched on, and how are pages fetched?', read: ['AI & OpenRouter tab (v2.15.301): Scholarship extraction (was Scholarships › Extraction) is below the AI configuration: cost today, the model order, any model waiting to be qualified or added, instructions and page answers. Curators see the extraction section only.', 'Fetchers tab (v2.15.300, was the Scrapers & fetchers page): the fetching services, their keys and their limits. Toolsets & limits starts with the course-page search budget (was on Scheduled jobs › Priority queue): this month\'s search credits and the monthly cap; when the cap is reached searches wait.', 'OpenRouter (Toolsets and limits, v2.15.258, bug 12/10-01): the balance (read from OpenRouter every 15 minutes by the openrouter-balance job), the credit floor, and for each AI use (scholarship AI, adapter builder, central pages AI, course matching) its calls and spend today (UTC) against its daily guard, plus the spend by day. Set to Observe: passing a guard or the floor raises a notice on the Layer 2 page and stops nothing; switched to stop at limits, the scholarship AI and central pages AI stop below the floor or past their guard. The old Layer 3 limits are retired.', 'Services, keys and limits, each in a card that is collapsed until opened (and stays as you leave it for the session), and whether each model passed its test.'], act: ['Switch a model on only after it passes its test (Platform Admin); anything off is offered nowhere else.'] },
  migration: { answers: 'What must pass before Production is switched on?', read: ['The go-live checklist.', 'Capacity (v2.15.301, was Platform health › Capacity): overview, capacity and performance, below the checklist.'], act: ['Platform Admin works the checklist.'] },
  users: { answers: 'Who can sign in, and what may each person do?', read: ['People, roles and expiry dates.', 'Deleted users: who was deleted, by whom and when.'], act: ['Give each person the lowest role that lets them do their job; use an expiry date for contractors (Platform Admin).', 'Disable stops sign-in and can be undone. Delete (Platform Admin) is final: type the email to confirm. A Platform Admin, your own account and the system automation account cannot be deleted. A user named on recorded work is kept in the background so the history stays linked; their roles end at once.'] },
}

export const SIGNALS = [
  { see: 'Automation failed: "took too long and was stopped by the database time limit"', where: 'Scheduled jobs', means: 'One run tried too much work', act: 'Lower "per run" by about a third; check the next run succeeds', who: 'Operator' },
  { see: 'The same automation failed 3 or more runs in a row with the same reason', where: 'Scheduled jobs', means: 'A real fault, not load', act: 'Pause it, note the reason, raise it with the platform engineer', who: 'Operator' },
  { see: 'OpenRouter credit approaching the floor', where: 'Platform health', means: 'Scholarship AI reading will stop at the floor', act: 'Top up the OpenRouter account the platform\'s key uses', who: 'Platform Admin' },
  // v2.15.253 (Platform Admin, 12 Oct 2026): credit and limit banner on every page
  { see: 'A coloured bar under the page title, scrolling sideways (red: critical, amber: warning)', where: 'Every page (Curator and above)', means: 'A credit or limit is low or used up: Firecrawl credits, OpenRouter credit, the adapter AI allowance or the scholarship scraper cap. Each notice starts with the tool\'s name; it is read again every 5 minutes and goes when the problem is fixed', act: 'Open Models & services from the bar and top up or raise the limit; × hides the bar until the page is reloaded', who: 'Platform Admin' },
  { see: 'A university stopped on Layer 2 › Onboarding', where: 'Layer 2 › Onboarding', means: 'Its automatic onboarding could not continue; the row says why (no website, too few course pages, sample pages not captured, AI proposal failed, adapter switched off, unexpected error)', act: 'Do what the row says, then tick it and Retry selected with a reason', who: 'Platform Admin' },
  { see: 'Firecrawl balance near the reserve', where: 'Platform health › budgets', means: 'Searches and reads stop to protect the reserve', act: 'Lower search pace, add credits, or wait for the monthly refresh', who: 'Platform Admin' },
  { see: 'A worker error repeating every run on Task manager › Background jobs (for example "invalid_pilot_automation_key")', where: 'Scheduled jobs › Task manager › Background jobs › Workers sending back errors', means: 'The job runs on time but its worker refuses the work, so nothing is done', act: 'Tell the Platform Admin. Every job now signs in with one-time run passes, so a refused old automation key means something outside the platform\'s own jobs is still sending it', who: 'Operator' },
  { see: 'A coloured notice at the top of a Layer page', where: 'Layers 1 to 4', means: 'A toolset that layer depends on hit a limit or timed out', act: 'Read the hint on the notice, change the setting on Models & services › Toolsets and limits if needed, then acknowledge it', who: 'Platform Admin' },
  { see: 'Layer 4 waiting count rises for 2 or more days', where: 'Dashboard, Layer 4', means: 'Reviewers are behind', act: 'Work oldest first; send repeat cases back to the AI with a reason', who: 'Curator' },
  { see: 'A coverage count flat for a day', where: 'Coverage', means: 'Its job is paused, failing or out of budget', act: 'Check that job in Scheduled jobs and the budgets check', who: 'Operator' },
  { see: 'A course link shown as gone', where: 'Course record, Link refresh', means: 'The provider page returns "not found"', act: 'It is searched for again automatically; fix by hand if the course has moved', who: 'Curator' },
  { see: 'A fee schedule waiting for approval', where: 'Adapter builder (1.3), or Layer 2 › Onboarding › Approvals waiting', means: 'Parsed fees are ready to add', act: 'Open the rows, check a few against the document, approve or reject', who: 'Platform Admin' },
  { see: 'A scholarship that was published is no longer on the website or in Zoho', where: 'Scholarships › Coverage', means: 'The daily publication review withdrew it because it no longer passes a check (closed, no longer offered, domestic only, no value)', act: 'Open its page; fix the record if the reading was wrong, then republish; otherwise leave it withdrawn', who: 'Platform Admin' },
  { see: 'A scholarship\'s value shows "Value not stated"', where: 'Scholarships, course record, Zoho', means: 'No value could be recorded from the page, so it cannot be published', act: 'Enter the value as the page states it on the record (kept as entered by hand), or leave it held', who: 'Curator' },
  { see: 'A saving marked as an estimate', where: 'Course record, Zoho', means: 'Worked out from the registered CRICOS course cost because the provider\'s annual fee is not recorded yet', act: 'Nothing; it is replaced when the provider fee is read. Quote it to students as an estimate', who: 'Counsellor' },
  { see: 'Ranked universities not linked in a country we hold', where: 'Rankings › QS or THE (Link: Not linked)', means: 'The names did not agree closely enough to link automatically', act: 'Link from the suggestions or a search, or mark "Not this one"', who: 'Curator' },
]

export const ADMIN_DUTIES = [
  { title: 'Approvals (daily)', items: ['Fee schedules: compare three or four rows against the provider\'s document, then approve.', 'Scholarships › Coverage: open three or four automatically published scholarships, compare the value and who it is for with the page, and Hold anything wrong.', 'Layer 2 › Onboarding: universities that stopped (retry once fixed) and Ready to admit (admit on Layer 2 › Adapters after checking the held reasons).', 'New AI models: switched on only after they pass the task\'s test.'] },
  { title: 'Budgets and keys (weekly)', items: ['Models & services has three tabs (v2.15.264): Services (switch page-fetching services and AI models on or off), AI & OpenRouter (the OpenRouter balance, mode, credit floor and the one OpenRouter key, set and verified there by a Platform Admin; each AI use with its model, daily guard and spend today; the central pages model and switch; the adapter proposal model; the scholarship AI models in order with Qualify and Make active; every model profile with its prompt version and hash) and Toolsets & limits (notices, Firecrawl budget and credits by university, the other toolsets). The AI settings Layer 3 used to hold are on AI & OpenRouter.', 'Firecrawl: monthly plan; the guard follows the balance Firecrawl reports and stops at the reserve.', 'OpenRouter: prepaid credit, observed rather than capped (Decision 252): the daily guards and the floor raise notices and stop nothing unless Models & services › Toolsets and limits is switched to stop at limits. OpenRouter refuses calls itself when the balance or the key\'s own limit runs out; the work is released and retried.', 'Notices: each Layer page shows a notice when a toolset it depends on hits a limit or times out (OpenRouter, Firecrawl, scheduled jobs, edge functions, sample runs, a key at its plan limit). Acknowledge it with a reason; it comes back if it happens again.', 'Serper and ScrapingBee: each runs on a key whose plan limits (plan name, credits, renewal, the date credits are counted from, credits kept back, calls at once) are settings on Models & services › Toolsets and limits. To move to a production key, replace the key on Settings and enter the new plan there. Sample runs take cases from each country and show results with a cost projection; nothing a sample run finds is admitted.', 'Search pass: Serper searches the courses still without a page and sends each page it finds on the provider\'s own site to the identity check, like any other page. A confirmed page or a link entered by hand is never replaced. Its limits are settings on Models & services › Toolsets and limits.', 'Supabase: project plan; screens stop a call after 8 seconds.', 'Keys live in Environment & keys and Models & services.', 'Every background job and worker signs in with a one-time run pass, made for each call and usable once within 5 minutes. A worker that calls another worker makes a fresh pass for each call. Only functions on the run-pass allow-list can be given one. The old long-lived automation key expired on 30 Sep 2026 and is accepted nowhere; there is no shared key to rotate.'] },
  { title: 'Users (as needed)', items: ['Lowest role that does the job; expiry dates for contractors.'] },
  { title: 'Adding a country', items: ['Load its register in Layer 1.', 'Set its admission rule (which identities are accepted for links, English and intakes, and its currency).', 'Add a link refresh schedule only if it needs a different pace.', 'Switch on its portal in Link refresh, if one exists.', 'Ranked universities in the new country link automatically within the hour.', 'Watch Coverage for two days before announcing it.'] },
]

